# broiler-shared-package pin 1
#
# One package of the committed, hash-pinned feed (decision SJL-D-4 (c); milestone SJL-2.7): a shared
# JavaScript library package whose home is the Broiler.JS repository, retained here byte for byte so
# that a restore needs no other repository's folder and no network for it. NuGet.config's package
# source mapping sends the Broiler.ECMAScript prefix to this directory and to nuget.org; the lock
# file of a project that references it records `content-hash`, and rule I1 holds that hash to this
# pin and to the allow-list.
#
# HOW IT WAS TAKEN. Packed on 2026-10-12 in the Broiler.JS repository, from `upstream-commit`, with
# `dotnet pack Broiler.ECMAScript/Broiler.ECMAScript.Algorithms -c Release -p:Version=<version>
# -p:PackageVersion=<version> -p:ContinuousIntegrationBuild=true`; the nuspec's repository element
# records the same commit, which rule I7 reads. `content-hash` is NuGet's: the base64 SHA-512 of the
# .nupkg's bytes, which is what a lock file records. `sha256` is over the same bytes.
#
# WHAT IT IS. The probe pre-release of milestone SJL-2.13: the contract types only (WorkCharge,
# ResultStatus, Failure, LengthLimit, DepthLimit), admitted TEST-ONLY for the admission probe of
# SJL-2.9. It is never published to nuget.org, and no product project references it.

id Broiler.ECMAScript.Algorithms
version 0.0.1-probe.1
file Broiler.ECMAScript.Algorithms.0.0.1-probe.1.nupkg
content-hash CCmUoN1rNXwTk7vTwNB3OoLDh2uk/zn3QRT4qfnnwBklqRKKcrS3sxxqUVBFW5Rv9el1OYl+e4OMnx230TvIrQ==
sha256 fa47374e1a7462304e2efd20504d13617eb88beed77fa3f5cb3ede25de360122
upstream Broiler-Platform/broiler.js
upstream-commit a84a0b4ccd9497d9a6cea03e64030e7c5ab6b0ad
